# fixedbugs, defect 2053, 2026-10-13, the reproducer, its words the Windows
# target's: judged there alone (`tests/harness/platform_skips.hero`), and
# its mark on every platform.
#
# SYMPTOM: on the Windows box (clang 23.1.1, MSVC target) a header of the
# program's own defining `hero_str_len` again as `static`, read as
# Microsoft's extension, built, and the link said `duplicate symbol:
# hero_str_len`, `internal error: linking failed`, exit 2. This Mac and
# Linux refused it at exit 1, `static declaration of 'hero_str_len' follows
# non-static declaration`.
#
# FIX: `-Wmicrosoft-redeclare-static` is an error in the header's region
# (`emit/header_region.hero`'s `EXTENDED`), so Windows refuses the header at
# its line 5, exit 1, its note told as the Heroes runtime's own name.

extern "fixedbugs-2053-a-header-that-defines-a-called-runtime-function-again-as-static-is-refused-on-windows.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    word = "abc"
    print(eight())
    print(word.len())
